From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:32:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 114/133] fix(polecat): single-quote the affected-tests test
 and flag unmapped go re-runs (gcp-oczc)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Self-review touch-ups to cb786ad4.

The `[ -n "{{affected_tests_command}}" ]` test double-quoted the rendered
command, so a command carrying $(...) was expanded (run) just to test that
it is non-empty, and a path with spaces could split it. It now uses the
same single quotes as the gate_run call beside it.

The base re-run in self-review §3 exits 0 when `go test -run` matches no
test at all ("[no tests to run]"), which would read as "green on base". It
errs toward "yours", the safe side, but the prose now says to fall back to
the whole phase command in that case. Exercised by hand on this rig's
module-root id go:..TestGastownEmbedsPackContent: it maps to
`go test ./. -run ^TestGastownEmbedsPackContent$` and runs that one test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml b/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
index a61cc327..c0665107 100644
--- a/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
+++ b/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
@@ -651,11 +651,12 @@ gate_run setup '{{setup_command}}'
 gate_run typecheck '{{typecheck_command}}'
 gate_run lint '{{lint_command}}'
 gate_run build '{{build_command}}'
-if [ -n "{{affected_tests_command}}" ]; then
+if [ -n '{{affected_tests_command}}' ]; then
     # Rig has an affected-tests detector. Run only the tests our diff
     # touches — same logic the rig's CI uses to dispatch test workflows.
     # The command must read `git diff --name-only origin/{{base_branch}}...HEAD`
-    # internally and execute the relevant test subset.
+    # internally and execute the relevant test subset. Single-quoted like
+    # gate_run's argument, so testing it never expands or runs any of it.
     gate_run affected-tests '{{affected_tests_command}}'
 else
     # No affected detector — run test_command as the rig configured it.
@@ -713,8 +714,10 @@ echo "re-run on base exit $? for $ID"
 git worktree remove --force "$T"
 ```
   Exit 0 means **green on base: the red is yours.** Fix it and re-run
-  self-review from §2. Non-zero means red on base; read the output to confirm
-  it is the same failure and not a re-run that could not start. Once every
+  self-review from §2. A go re-run that printed `[no tests to run]` did not
+  map the id: re-run the whole phase through `PHASE_CMD` instead. Non-zero
+  means red on base; read the output to confirm it is the same failure and not
+  a re-run that could not start. Once every
   NEW id that remains is red on base too, record them, then proceed:
 ```bash
 KR='<the known-red path the §2 block printed>'
